# Copy to .env.frontends. Read by the three PUBLIC sites in the `frontends`
# compose profile (landingpage, blog, tools) — not by the panels, which
# authenticate as a person via the session cookie and have no page cache.
#
# Both values are optional. Without them the sites still work: content reads
# stay open unless an admin switched site-key enforcement on, and the cache
# control plane answers 503 so nothing can trigger a rebuild.
#
# Why a separate file and not .env.docker: Compose interpolates `${…}` in the
# compose file out of the project's ./.env, which in this repo is the gateway
# app's own config for `composer start`. Anything put in .env.docker for these
# would have silently become an empty string. .env.docker stays what it is —
# the API container's env_file.

# Issued in the admin panel under Einstellungen → Site-Verbindungen. Shown once
# and stored only as a SHA-256 hash: lost means reissue, not look up.
TDS_SITE_KEY=

# Freely chosen. Must match what you enter in the panel for each site's page
# cache, because the direction is reversed here: the API calls the site.
TDS_CACHE_TOKEN=

# --- when one value per site is not enough ---------------------------------
# The three sites share this file. Once site-key enforcement is on, each site
# needs its OWN key — put it in .env.landingpage, .env.blog or .env.tools
# (same two variable names, optional files, loaded after this one).
